    id: 'arrays', title: 'Arrays', concept: 'int a[5]',
    body: '<p>An <b>array</b> is a fixed-size row of values of the same type: <code>int a[3] = {10, 20, 30};</code>. Positions start at <b>0</b>, so the last valid index is size - 1.</p><p>C does not remember an array\'s size once you pass it to a function, so pass the size too. Reading past the end is a classic bug (undefined behaviour). This editor stops you with a clear message instead of crashing.</p>',
