    body: '<p>A well-designed class protects its own rules. Here the balance is <code>private</code>, so outside code cannot set it to nonsense. <code>withdraw</code> <b>throws</b> when the request is not allowed, and the caller decides how to respond with <code>try</code> / <code>catch</code>.</p><p>This combination (private data, a small public interface, exceptions for misuse) is the backbone of well-structured C++.</p>',
